{"key":"i07-s0002","rationale":"Idea:\nThe `spiking_fla_gated_residual` architecture builds upon the robust `LightNet` and the refined `SpikingMLP` of Version 2 by re-introducing and enhancing spike-gated residual connections. This design directly addresses the ","callouts":{"1":"Intermediate spiking neuron: fc1's analog output drives a LIF layer instead of GELU, and fc2 receives its (dropped-out) binary spikes.","2":"Spike-rate residual gates: the per-token firing rate (mean over channels) of the k-projection spikes, or of the three MLP spike trains, drives a spiking layer 1 → d whose output gives γ ⊙ σ(·) (γ learnable, init 1); the branch is multiplied by it before the residual add."},"notes":[{"text":"dropout on spikes","kind":"evolved"}],"meta":"Iteration 7 · sample 2  ·  LightNet state update","nodes":{"n1":{"label":"RMSNorm","code":"L283","tip":null},"q":{"label":"q proj","code":"L168","tip":null},"k":{"label":"k proj","code":"L169","tip":null},"v":{"label":"v proj","code":"L170","tip":null},"gp":{"label":"g proj","code":"L171","tip":null},"ws":{"label":"logσ","code":"L190","tip":null},"core":{"label":"Gated recurrence","code":"L45-L156","tip":null},"onorm":{"label":"RMSNorm","code":"L206","tip":null},"oproj":{"label":"o proj","code":"L207","tip":null},"rate1":{"label":"spike rate","code":"L293-L295","tip":null,"novel":2},"rg1":{"label":"rate gate","code":"L305-L307","tip":null,"novel":2},"gm1":{"label":"×","code":"L308","tip":null,"novel":2},"a1":{"label":"+","code":"L310","tip":null},"n2":{"label":"RMSNorm","code":"L314","tip":null},"fc1":{"label":"fc1","code":"L229","tip":null},"lif":{"label":"LIF","code":"L234-L236","tip":null,"novel":1},"fc2":{"label":"fc2","code":"L246","tip":null},"rate2":{"label":"spike rate","code":"L323-L331","tip":null,"novel":2},"rg2":{"label":"rate gate","code":"L332-L334","tip":null,"novel":2},"gm2":{"label":"×","code":"L335","tip":null,"novel":2},"a2":{"label":"+","code":"L337","tip":null},"core/dec":{"label":"exp","code":"L57,L